From 547c84b64d84a4fa8982a0d14657a85956152eb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r7b <r7b@parity>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:43:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] targeting.HIDDEN_HOLD_REACH = client16402_any_reach: a
 projectile attacker holding a Tesla that goes under keeps it past its keep
 reach

Mechanic: target.rs decide, under hide.HELD_THROUGH_HIDE, kept a building gone under ground for a melee walker always but for
a projectile attacker only within Range + LOGIC_RANGE_EXTENSION_TO_KEEP_TARGET; past that it rescanned at once (a scan never
takes a building under). New arm client16402_any_reach (shipped): every holder keeps it, the reach unread;
HELD_THROUGH_HIDE's own clock (client16402_kept_hide_time: its HideTimeMs under) still ends the hold. Old arm
projectile_keep_reach; CLIENT15535_ARMS keeps it; format-3 snapshots keep it. Plant hold_reach_dropped. Fixture:
tests/hidden_hold_reach.rs (tests/hide.rs's Giant scene with a Royal Giant pinned 7000 off, past its 5000 Range).

Parity-Evidence: ClashBot diag_night/r7b holdcen.py, 266 upgraded captured 16.402 logs with phase-3 attack rows: projectile
attackers naming a Tesla on its last frame up and standing past Range + 500 of its edge let it go 12-20 ticks after its
first frame under (after its attack 5 of 5 drops, after its deploy 10 of 11, 1 at 4-11), never within 3 ticks; in reach 37
at 12-20, 2 within 3. liveplay 20261017_235525 t2664: a Royal Giant 5.7 tiles off our just-deployed Tesla holds it 17 ticks
under, then takes the princess tower; the engine took the tower at once (K=0 death tick 2828 -> 2816 = live).
